  "traps": [
    "eShop.AppHost has no ProjectReference: it launches each service with AddDotnetProject(\"basket-api\", \"../Basket.API\") by folder path, so its depends_on is empty and the orchestration lives only in src/eShop.AppHost/AppHost.cs",
    "three solutions: eShop.slnx (all 28 projects), src/ClientApp/ClientApp.sln (ClientApp and its tests) and tests/ClientApp.UnitTests/ClientApp.UnitTests.sln; eShop.Web.slnf is a solution filter over eShop.slnx that drops HybridApp, ClientApp and ClientApp.UnitTests, and it is what CI builds (pr-validation.yml, ci.yml)",
    "central package management: PackageReference carries no Version and the version is in Directory.Packages.props (declared_in stays the csproj, as in mix-dotnet-central); ClientApp, HybridApp and ClientApp.UnitTests set ManagePackageVersionsCentrally=false and write their own versions, so HybridApp asks Microsoft.Maui.Controls 9.0.30 and ClientApp.UnitTests 9.0.40",
    "no packages.lock.json: every NuGet resolved is null; only the root package-lock.json fixes the three npm versions",
    "MSTest.Sdk 4.0.2 (global.json msbuild-sdks) and Aspire.AppHost.Sdk/13.6.0 (the Sdk attribute of eShop.AppHost and the four functional test projects) are MSBuild project SDKs fetched from NuGet like build plugins: they are build dependencies of those projects, not toolchains; aspire.config.json repeats sdk 13.6.0 for the Aspire CLI and .aspire/settings.json only points the CLI at the AppHost",
    "global.json asks SDK 10.0.302 with rollForward latestFeature and allowPrerelease false, while .config/configuration.*.winget installs Microsoft.DotNet.SDK.Preview with no version; pr-validation workflows and ci.yml take the SDK from global.json, playwright.yml asks 10.0.x",
    "TargetFramework net10.0 is not a toolchain; ClientApp and HybridApp list target frameworks, add net10.0-windows10.0.19041.0 only when building on Windows, and keep tizen commented out, so src/HybridApp/Platforms/Tizen/Main.cs is never compiled; each Platforms/<os> folder compiles only for its target framework",
    "the MAUI workloads (android, ios, maccatalyst, maui) are installed by pr-validation-maui.yml with no version pinned; SupportedOSPlatformVersion values are platform API minimums, not toolchains",
    "src/Shared has no project: ActivityExtensions.cs and MigrateDbContextExtensions.cs are compiled into five projects through Compile Include with Link",
    "the gRPC contract basket.proto exists twice: src/Basket.API/Proto/basket.proto (Server, and Client for WebApp, which includes it across folders) and a copy in src/ClientApp/Services/Basket/Protos with another csharp_namespace; ClientApp sets CompileOutputs=false and OutputDir empty, so the protoc output Basket.cs and BasketGrpc.cs is checked in and compiled by the default glob",
    "integration events have no shared contract project: each service declares its own record with the same type name, and RabbitMQEventBus routes on @event.GetType().Name over the exchange eshop_event_bus; publisher and subscribers are joined only by that string",
    "PaymentProcessor and WebApp call AddRabbitMqEventBus(\"EventBus\") while the AppHost resource is \"eventbus\": .NET configuration keys are case-insensitive, so it binds",
    "OrderProcessor reads the table ordering.orders straight from orderingdb with Npgsql: it shares the database of Ordering.API without any project reference, and the AppHost makes it wait for ordering-api because that service runs the migrations",
    "Redis is the store of record of baskets (StringSetAsync in Basket.API), not a cache; PostgreSQL runs the image ankane/pgvector because Catalog.API stores embeddings with Pgvector",
    "Azure OpenAI (Foundry deployments gpt-4.1-mini and text-embedding-3-small) is wired only when configuration enables Foundry, and Ollama only behind the constant useOllama = false; both are named in code, not in a compose file",
    "the Android manifest carries the placeholder Google Maps key YOUR_KEY_GOES_HERE",
    "the mobile clients reach catalog and orders through the YARP resource mobile-bff at port 11632, a port written only in ClientApp and HybridApp; ClientApp also calls l/api/v1/locations, which no service in the repository serves",
    "src/Catalog.API/Catalog.API.json and Catalog.API_v2.json are OpenAPI documents written at build by Microsoft.Extensions.ApiDescription.Server into the project folder (OpenApiDocumentsDirectory); site.min.js is the empty output of bundleconfig.json and _references.js is Visual Studio's autosync list",
    "EF Core migrations: the *.Designer.cs and *ModelSnapshot.cs files carry // <auto-generated /> and are generated; the migration classes themselves have no header and are hand-owned source",
    "AnyFutureIntegrationEventHandler.cs.txt is C# text disabled by its extension; OrderPaymentFailedIntegrationEvent .cs has a space before the extension and still compiles",
    "Identity.API restores jQuery, Bootstrap and jquery-validation into wwwroot/lib at build through libman.json and Microsoft.Web.LibraryManager.Build; the folder is not in the repository",
    "the root package.json is a private npm package for the Playwright tests in e2e/, with no workspaces and no tsconfig: Playwright transpiles the TypeScript itself; its webServer runs dotnet run on the AppHost",
    "eShop.slnx lists NuGet.config while the file is nuget.config: it resolves only on a case-insensitive file system",
    ".github/skills holds Markdown skills for coding agents, not project documentation of the code, and is excluded as documentation"
